1. **A computer-implemented system for customer sentiment analysis in a call center environment**, comprising:  
   one or more processors;  
   one or more memory devices storing executable instructions;  
   a speech analytics engine configured to receive and process audio data from a voice interaction between a customer and a call center agent;  
   a transcription module configured to convert at least a portion of the audio data into text;  
   an acoustic feature extraction module configured to identify one or more non-lexical speech characteristics, including at least tone, pitch, speaking rate, silence duration, interruption frequency, or volume variation;  
   an omnichannel data ingestion module configured to receive customer interaction data from a plurality of communication channels including at least one of voice calls, chat messages, email messages, SMS messages, social media interactions, web forms, mobile application interactions, or customer relationship management records;  
   a sentiment analysis module configured to generate a customer sentiment score based on both the transcribed text and the acoustic feature data; and  
   a customer experience analytics module configured to correlate the customer sentiment score with the omnichannel customer interaction data to determine an overall customer sentiment state associated with a customer journey.

2. **The system of claim 1**, wherein the sentiment analysis module comprises a machine learning model trained on historical call center interactions labeled with sentiment, emotion, intent, escalation outcome, customer satisfaction score, or churn risk.

3. **The system of claim 1**, wherein the customer sentiment score includes at least one of a positive sentiment indicator, a negative sentiment indicator, a neutral sentiment indicator, an emotional intensity value, a frustration score, a satisfaction score, or a churn probability.

4. **The system of claim 1**, wherein the omnichannel data ingestion module normalizes customer interaction data from the plurality of communication channels into a unified customer interaction timeline.

5. **The system of claim 4**, wherein the customer experience analytics module determines a change in customer sentiment over time by comparing sentiment values associated with multiple interactions in the unified customer interaction timeline.

6. **The system of claim 1**, further comprising an agent assistance module configured to generate, in real time during the voice interaction, at least one recommended agent action based on the customer sentiment score and the omnichannel customer interaction data.

7. **The system of claim 6**, wherein the recommended agent action includes at least one of a suggested response, escalation recommendation, retention offer, compliance prompt, empathy prompt, supervisor alert, or knowledge-base article.

8. **The system of claim 1**, wherein the speech analytics engine is further configured to detect overlapping speech, customer silence, agent silence, stress markers, or emotional cues within the voice interaction.

9. **The system of claim 1**, wherein the sentiment analysis module applies natural language processing to identify sentiment-bearing terms, customer intent, topic category, complaint type, resolution status, or named entities within the transcribed text.

10. **The system of claim 1**, wherein the customer experience analytics module generates a risk score representing a likelihood that the customer will cancel a service, lodge a complaint, request escalation, provide a negative survey response, or discontinue engagement with an enterprise.

11. **A computer-implemented method for analyzing customer sentiment in a call center**, comprising:  
    receiving audio data corresponding to a voice interaction between a customer and a call center agent;  
    converting at least a portion of the audio data into text using automated speech recognition;  
    extracting, from the audio data, acoustic features indicative of customer emotion or sentiment;  
    receiving omnichannel customer interaction data associated with the customer from a plurality of communication channels;  
    generating, by a sentiment analysis model, a sentiment score based on the text and the acoustic features;  
    correlating the sentiment score with the omnichannel customer interaction data to produce an overall customer sentiment state; and  
    outputting the overall customer sentiment state to at least one call center application.

12. **The method of claim 11**, further comprising generating a real-time alert when the sentiment score satisfies a threshold condition indicating negative sentiment, elevated frustration, escalation risk, or churn risk.

13. **The method of claim 11**, further comprising updating a customer profile with the overall customer sentiment state and storing the updated customer profile in a customer relationship management system.

14. **The method of claim 11**, wherein correlating the sentiment score with the omnichannel customer interaction data comprises weighting sentiment signals from different channels according to recency, interaction type, customer value, interaction duration, or detected issue severity.

15. **The method of claim 11**, further comprising identifying a root cause of negative sentiment based on detected conversation topics and historical interaction data.

16. **The method of claim 11**, wherein the sentiment analysis model generates separate sentiment outputs for the customer and the agent and compares the separate sentiment outputs to determine conversation alignment or mismatch.

17. **The method of claim 11**, further comprising generating a post-call summary including customer sentiment, key topics, unresolved issues, recommended follow-up actions, and a predicted customer satisfaction outcome.

18. **The method of claim 11**, wherein the omnichannel customer interaction data includes prior chat transcripts, email content, customer survey results, purchase history, service ticket history, web browsing activity, mobile application events, or social media posts.

19. **A non-transitory computer-readable medium storing instructions that, when executed by one or more processors, cause the one or more processors to perform operations comprising:**  
    obtaining call audio from a customer-agent interaction;  
    performing speech-to-text transcription on the call audio;  
    extracting acoustic emotion indicators from the call audio;  
    obtaining omnichannel interaction records associated with the customer;  
    applying a trained sentiment analysis model to the transcription, the acoustic emotion indicators, and the omnichannel interaction records;  
    generating a unified sentiment assessment for the customer; and  
    causing presentation of the unified sentiment assessment in a call center interface.

20. **The non-transitory computer-readable medium of claim 19**, wherein the operations further comprise automatically prioritizing the customer for follow-up, escalation, retention treatment, or quality assurance review based on the unified sentiment assessment.
